# Drafted by Gemini (R16 farewell), edited.

~ morgan_thanks
morgan [weary]: You did it. The fever broke just before the bell, and the colour is coming back into their cheeks.
morgan [smile]: Half the cots are already sitting up and asking after broth. I set these vials aside for the four of you, mixed for strong hearts and bad air.
give potion_of_healing_greater 2
give potion_of_resistance_poison 1
quest skitter_plague back_in_wickermoor
quest skitter_plague done
set skitter_farewell
set act2_done += 1
xp milestone
Narrator: The bitter stink of black bile has gone from the room, replaced by bruised mint, clean linen, and the quiet clink of warm glass.
-> menu

~ menu
* Ask how the sick are -> sick
* Ask what Morgan remembers -> remembers
* Take our leave -> bye

~ sick
morgan [smile]: Old Haldor called for salted turnips the moment his eyes opened, and Ottilie's little one slept through the hour without a whimper. Even Pim Fenwick stopped groaning long enough to ask for his mirror.
-> bye

~ remembers
morgan [weary]: I reached back for it while the kettle boiled, some face or song from before the mist took me. There was only quiet water, and for once I did not mind.
-> bye

~ bye
morgan [smile]: Go easy on the road, friends. The kettle is on whenever you pass the door.
-> END

~ reopening
appear phillip_druskenvald
appear wendel_somerton
cutscene sk_reopening
cutscene sk_reopening_2
wendel_somerton [smile]: Behold, my dear friends, the charter of reclamation, the timber tallies, and the preliminary pit-head requisitions! Glitterdeep Mine shall live again, properly stamped and witnessed!
phillip_druskenvald [smile]: Say, the old house is footing the whole bill, top to bottom. Once these good folks have their sea legs back, every able hand in Wickermoor has a wage waiting up the hill.
wendel_somerton [smile]: Most remarkable of all, Miss Mayville delivered a sealed notice of congratulation from the post office before I had even dipped my pen.
cutscene end
* Ask Phillip about the funding -> funding
* Ask Wendel about the forms -> forms
* Wish them luck -> luck

~ funding
phillip_druskenvald [weary]: A gentleman squares his ledger, old sport, even when the ink is seventy years dry. My family has owed this valley a clean pit and an honest living for a very long time.
-> end_node

~ forms
wendel_somerton [smile]: Everything is drawn up in triplicate for the new signboard, though I remain agonizingly torn between restoring Glitterdeep and inaugurating the New Somerton Delve.
-> end_node

~ luck
wendel_somerton [smile]: May the Green Queen bless the beams and keep the dark beneath the stone.
-> end_node

~ end_node
set glitterdeep_reopening
-> END
